Exports the bodies bc2cpp's closed `%` and `-@` helpers (tools/bc2cpp/
codegen_numeric_slow.rb) run for a proven receiver class, so the generated C++
calls them directly instead of dispatching by name (docs/adr/0367):

  src/numeric.c                          mrb_int_mod_impl, mrb_flo_mod_impl
  mruby-string-ext/src/string.c          mrb_str_uminus_impl
  mruby-sprintf/src/sprintf.c            mrb_str_format_impl

The three method bodies moved into the exported `*_impl` function, which takes
its argument explicitly; int_mod, flo_mod and str_uminus stay registered and
only read their argument (`mrb_get_arg1`) and call it, so interpreted behaviour
is unchanged. mrb_str_format already took explicit arguments, so its export is
a forwarding function. No header changes: the generated code declares them with
extern "C" itself, and it checks the registered wrapper's text before it relies
on one, so a tree without this patch keeps the by-name helpers.

